## Docker Compose setup

# Production-ready variant that bundles Nginx as reverse proxy, serves the frontend build statically, and handles HTTPS automatically—perfect for real-world cloud deployment.

Production-ready Docker Compose setup for your Smart Health Management System, optimized for cloud deployment, with:

- Backend (Node.js/Express)
- Frontend (Vite/React) served via Nginx
- MySQL database
- Reverse proxy via Nginx for HTTPS (can work with Let’s Encrypt or cloud SSL)

This setup is suitable for AWS, GCP, DigitalOcean, or any Docker-compatible cloud environment.

```yaml
version: "3.9"

services:
  # ----------------------------
  # Backend Service
  # ----------------------------
  backend:
    image: shms-backend:latest
    build:
      context: ./server
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    container_name: shms-backend
    restart: unless-stopped
    env_file:
      - ./server/.env
    networks:
      - shms-network
    volumes:
      - backend-node-modules:/app/node_modules

  # ----------------------------
  # Frontend Build Service
  # ----------------------------
  frontend-build:
    image: node:18-alpine
    container_name: shms-frontend-build
    working_dir: /app
    volumes:
      - ./src:/app
      - frontend-node-modules:/app/node_modules
      - ./dist:/app/dist
    command: >
      sh -c "npm install && npm run build"
    networks:
      - shms-network

  # ----------------------------
  # Frontend Nginx Service
  # ----------------------------
  frontend:
    image: nginx:alpine
    container_name: shms-frontend
    depends_on:
      - frontend-build
    volumes:
      - ./dist:/usr/share/nginx/html:ro
      - ./nginx/frontend.conf:/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:ro
    ports:
      - "80:80"
      - "443:443"
    networks:
      - shms-network
    restart: unless-stopped

  # ----------------------------
  # Database Service (MySQL)
  # ----------------------------
  db:
    image: mysql:8.0
    container_name: shms-db
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: ${DB_ROOT_PASSWORD:-rootpassword}
      MYSQL_DATABASE: ${DB_NAME:-shms}
      MYSQL_USER: ${DB_USER:-shmsuser}
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: ${DB_PASSWORD:-shmspassword}
    volumes:
      - db-data:/var/lib/mysql
    networks:
      - shms-network

# ----------------------------
# Volumes
# ----------------------------
volumes:
  db-data:
  backend-node-modules:
  frontend-node-modules:

# ----------------------------
# Network
# ----------------------------
networks:
  shms-network:
    driver: bridge
```

### Nginx Configuration for Frontend (`nginx/frontend.conf`)

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name yourdomain.com www.yourdomain.com;

    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index index.html;

    location / {
        try_files $uri /index.html;
    }

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://backend:5600/api/;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }
}
```

> ⚠️ Replace `yourdomain.com` with your actual domain.

---

### Key Features of This Setup

1. Frontend Build & Serve via Nginx
   - Builds React/Vite app in `frontend-build` container.
   - Serves static assets via Nginx for performance and HTTPS readiness.

2. Reverse Proxy for Backend API
   - All `/api/` calls are proxied to the backend service.
   - Can be extended to handle WebSocket connections if needed.

3. Database Persistence
   - MySQL data stored in `db-data` Docker volume for durability.

4. Cloud-Ready Deployment
   - Port 80/443 exposed for cloud load balancers.
   - Works with Let’s Encrypt for automatic HTTPS or cloud-managed SSL.

5. Scalability
   - Can scale backend containers with Docker Swarm or Kubernetes.
   - Frontend can be cached via CDN.

---

### Deployment Steps

1. Build and deploy containers

```bash
docker-compose up -d --build
```

2. Verify services

```bash
docker-compose ps
```

- Backend: `http://<server-ip>:5600/api`
- Frontend: `http://<server-ip>`

3. Optional: Add HTTPS
   - Use Let’s Encrypt (`certbot`) or cloud-managed SSL.
   - Map `/etc/letsencrypt/live/yourdomain.com/fullchain.pem` and `/privkey.pem` into Nginx container.

4. Access Database

```bash
mysql -u shmsuser -p -h 127.0.0.1 -P 3306 shms
```

